Subject: Build the upstream gtest suite as C++14 in the test directory only
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
Description: Set the test/ targets to C++14 so the packaged gtest 1.16 compiles, and keep the console_bridge library at the C++11 standard set in CMakeLists.txt.
Base-Tree: debian console-bridge 1.0.1+dfsg2-3
Verify: test test/CMakeLists.txt
Forwarded: not-needed (Debian leaves BUILD_TESTING off, so this change only affects DHI's test build)
Drop-When: never: packaged gtest 1.16 requires C++14 while the top-level CMakeLists.txt compiles every target with -std=c++11

Debian's 0002 patch points test/ at the packaged gtest sources, and those need C++14. The top-level CMakeLists.txt appends -std=c++11 to every target, so gtest 1.16 stops with "#error C++ versions less than C++14 are not supported". This patch sets the standard only in test/, before the gtest targets are created, so the shipped library is still compiled as C++11 like Debian's build.

--- a/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 )
 
 
+set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 14)
+set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
+set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF)
+
 # Build gtest
 add_library(gtest STATIC /usr/src/gtest/src/gtest-all.cc)
 target_include_directories(gtest
